body:
This PR introduces `createHits()`, available from `instantsearch-ui-components`. This method can be used by the Hits widget from each flavor to setup a UI component that renders appropriately.

## Design considerations

The UI component expects from widgets the following props:

```tsx
export type HitsProps<THit> = React.ComponentProps<'div'> & {
  hits: THit[];
  itemComponent: (props: {
    hit: THit;
    index: number;
    className: string;
    onClick: () => void;
    onAuxClick: () => void;
  }) => JSX.Element;
  sendEvent: SendEventForHits;
  classNames?: Partial<HitsClassNames>;
  emptyComponent?: (props: { className: string }) => JSX.Element;
};
```

**`itemComponent`**

Used by the component as a direct child of an `<ol>`. Widgets use this to wrap the item template / hit component / item slot.

**`classNames`**

The class list is from IS.js/RISH. Vue's component maps its specific structure to the more common one.

**`emptyComponent`**

When provided, the component renders this instead of returning an empty list if there are no hits. Only IS.js has this currently.

